        "original_id": "0cd1f4be-41b8-5d5a-b455-e0658fd02d31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Joseph J. Thorndike, Paige Rense\n- Products: American Heritage, Bon Appétit, Life, Horizon, GEO, Manor House\n- Companies: Condé Nast\n- Topics: U.S. history magazines, food and entertaining magazines\n\nFacts:\n- In the late 1940s, Joseph J. Thorndike was Managing Editor of Life for three years.\n- Joseph J. Thorndike co-founded the magazines American Heritage and Horizon.\n- American Heritage is a magazine dedicated to covering the history of the United States for a mainstream readership.\n- Paige Rense founded the cookery magazine Bon Appétit.\n- Bon Appétit is an American food and entertaining magazine published monthly by Condé Nast.\n- Paige Rense was editor in chief of GEO.\n- In 1997, Paige Rense published the mystery novel Manor House with Doubleday.",
